# Typed by hand from T. M. Krachan, PhD dissertation, Lviv (2018), section 3.2.11, Table 3.33 (cell, powder
# Rietveld, DRON-3M Cu Ka; a = 0.42119(1), b = 1.24388(4), c = 0.98361(3) nm) and Table 3.34 (coordinates, site
# mixtures per cell, B_iso x 10^2 nm^2 = A^2). Thesis ref. [200] is Krachan et al. J. Alloys Compd. 349 (2003) 134,
# the Y-Cu-Al paper cited for 0615, which was not accessible. Not from an ICDD card (04-012-4027, Y3Al8.5Cu2.5,
# same setting and a cell equal to these values within 1e-3 A, so it is very likely the same refinement).
# Site mixtures per cell -> occupancies: X1 2c 0.08 Cu/1.92 Al; X2 4j 0.52 Cu/3.48 Al; X4 8l 3.30 Cu/4.70 Al.
# Composition from these occupancies Y3Cu1.95Al9.05 (the thesis formula Y3Cu1.98Al9.02 is rounded).
# U = B/(8 pi^2). Mixed sites are written as Al/Cu pairs at one position (the driver's --partner-sites form).

